course: dictionary
lesson: 3615
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word film is a good example. «Films show piranhas stripping a cow in seconds» uses film to mean a movie, a story shown with moving pictures.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The deepest fish ever filmed was a snailfish» uses the verb filmed. The clue is that a fish was recorded, so filmed must mean recorded with a camera.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «A thin film of oil floated on the water» cannot mean a movie, because oil does not show a story. A thin layer fits, so that is the meaning. If your meaning still makes sense, you have probably chosen well.
fact: Film can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action): films, filmed, filming.
fact: «Film» as a noun means a movie, a story shown with moving pictures.
fact: «To film» means to record moving pictures with a camera.
fact: «Film» can also mean a thin layer, like «a film of oil» on water.
fact: Old cameras used a roll of film for photos, and a roll often had only 24 or 36 pictures.
exercise: «Films show piranhas stripping a cow in seconds.» What does film mean here? | *A movie, a story shown with moving pictures | To record with a camera | A thin layer of oil | A roll for an old camera
exercise: «The deepest fish ever filmed was a snailfish.» What does filmed mean? | Covered with a thin layer | Developed with chemicals in a dark room | Watched at the cinema | *Recorded moving pictures with a camera
exercise: «A thin film of oil floated on the water.» What does film mean here? | To record with a camera | *A thin layer | A roll for taking photos | A movie with actors
test: «Before digital cameras, photos were taken on film that had to be developed with chemicals.» What does film mean here? | A thin layer of oil | To record moving pictures | A movie shown in a cinema | *A roll used in old cameras to take photos
test: «Ratings are decided by trained examiners, not by the film makers.» What are film makers? | People who sell tickets at the cinema | *People who make movies | People who cover water with oil | People who develop photos in a dark room
exam: «Stunt performers are trained professionals, and film stunts must never be copied.» What does film stunts mean? | Stunts with a roll of pictures | Stunts done in a thin layer of oil | *Stunts performed in movies | Stunts for old cameras
